  "problem": "The concentration of a medication in a patient's bloodstream, measured in milligrams per liter, is given by the function $C(t)$, where $t$ is the time, in hours, since the medication was taken. The values of $C(t)$ for different values of $t$ are given in the table below:\n\n| $t$ | $1$ | $5$ | $9$ | $14$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $C(t)$ | $18$ | $11$ | $7$ | $2$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of the concentration when $t=9$ using a backward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nThe estimated rate of change when $t=9$ is\n{{field-1}} milligrams per liter per hour.",
